== Honey Cider Vinaigrette ==

Place @apple cider{1/3%cup}(not apple juice), @honey{1/3%cup}, @apple cider vinegar{3%tablespoons}, @salt{1/4%teaspoon} and @pepper{1/8%teaspoon} in a #blender{} and blend until honey is incorporated into mixture (you may need to scrape the bottom of the blender).

With lid on and blender speed running on low, slowly drizzle in the @extra virgin olive oil{3/4%cup}(or a vegetable oil, like canola) in a small steady stream until fully incorporated.

If desired, add additional salt and pepper to taste. You can also add a little more vinegar if you'd like it tangier...it's flexible!

== Salad ==

Place @greens{1%large bag}(spring mix, spinach mix, etc.) in large #serving bowl{} and top with @apples{1-2%medium}(sliced or diced), @butternut squash{1}(diced and roasted), @candied pecans{1%handful}(or other nut of your choice), @pepitas{1%handful}, @feta cheese{1%handful}(crumbled), @pomegranate arils{1%handful}, @red onion{1%small}(sliced thin), and @?roasted chicken{some}(shredded or diced).

> For the butternut squash: dice and roast before adding to the salad.

Toss with dressing and enjoy.